        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: generic criterion matching returned nil for CF-typed attributes",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nGeneric criteria fetched values through `Attribute<Any>`, whose typed conversion could return nil for real Core Foundation-backed accessibility values. A window with a readable `AXTitle` therefore failed an exact `AXRole` + `AXTitle` lookup.\n\n## Fix\n\nRead the raw AX attribute and normalize it through AXorcist's existing `ValueUnwrapper`, retaining the typed accessor as a fallback. This preserves string, boolean, number, and AXValue semantics while fixing generic matching. Add focused automation regression coverage and an Unreleased changelog entry thanking @dalsoop.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Current `main`: exact `AXWindow` + `AXTitle` lookup against a signed nine-node AppKit fixture returned not found and exited 1.\n- Repaired branch: the same lookup returned `Role: AXWindow, Title: 'AXorcist Probe'` and exited 0.\n- Negative control: `Wrong Probe Title` returned not found after nine nodes and exited 1.\n- `swift build`\n- `swift test --filter AXErrorExtensionsTests`\n- `swift test --filter ElementSearchTests` (automation suite compiled and was correctly skipped without the automation opt-in)\n- Structured autoreview: no actionable findings.\n- Exact-head CI: [run 29659361988](https://github.com/openclaw/AXorcist/actions/runs/29659361988) passed build, safe tests, lint, and release packaging.\n",
